1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,945
Cannot sign in: locks,
disabled accounts and timeouts.

2
00:00:03,945 --> 00:00:09,345
Distinguish an account lock from network
throttling, and know when to restart or

3
00:00:09,345 --> 00:00:11,568
contact your administrator.

4
00:00:13,155 --> 00:00:17,513
Repeated wrong passwords or
verification codes can lock an account.

5
00:00:17,513 --> 00:00:21,230
Stop guessing and read the
message MERIT gives you.

6
00:00:22,221 --> 00:00:24,783
The account is locked for fifteen minutes.

7
00:00:24,783 --> 00:00:29,297
Wait until it unlocks or ask an
administrator to unlock it after verifying

8
00:00:29,297 --> 00:00:30,605
your identity.

9
00:00:30,905 --> 00:00:34,151
Even a correct password
does not bypass the lock.

10
00:00:34,151 --> 00:00:37,598
A password-reset link
also does not bypass it.

11
00:00:38,792 --> 00:00:43,699
After the wait or a confirmed unlock,
start again with the correct password and

12
00:00:43,699 --> 00:00:45,099
authenticator.

13
00:00:49,962 --> 00:00:53,932
A disabled or unknown account
gets a general sign-in error.

14
00:00:53,932 --> 00:00:59,581
If the details are correct but access
still fails, contact your administrator.

15
00:01:00,188 --> 00:01:03,005
A sign-in verification page can expire.

16
00:01:03,005 --> 00:01:09,401
If MERIT sends you back to sign in, enter
your password again and use a fresh code.

17
00:01:11,320 --> 00:01:14,956
Too many attempts from one
network is a separate limit.

18
00:01:14,956 --> 00:01:20,579
This training instance demonstrates that
message without affecting other users.

19
00:01:28,317 --> 00:01:32,658
Wait for the number of seconds
shown, then use Back to sign in.

20
00:01:32,658 --> 00:01:38,087
Repeated retries do not remove either
a network limit or an account lock.

21
00:01:38,457 --> 00:01:44,108
If the problem continues, tell support
which message you see and your user name.

22
00:01:44,108 --> 00:01:49,806
Do not send your password, setup key,
recovery codes or verification codes.

23
00:01:53,419 --> 00:01:58,064
In this video you recognized account
locks and network throttling,

24
00:01:58,064 --> 00:02:03,202
restarted an expired verification
step, and identified when to contact an

25
00:02:03,202 --> 00:02:04,602
administrator.
